    {
      "line": 665,
      "text": "中文读题：比较三年每股收益 EPS（定义与分母见 §2.1.1）和行业水平。核对基本 / 稀释 EPS、财年、拆股调整与同业汇总方法；每股数值不能与未拆股价格混配。无年报和行业数据，受阻。"
    },
    {
      "line": 703,
      "text": "中文：毛利为收入减销售成本；营业利润（operating income）还扣除销售、管理、研发等运营费用；净利润再考虑利息、税等。分别把这三个利润额除同期收入，不混用口径。利润率从 30% 到 25% 是下降 5 个百分点，不能写成下降 5%。英文参考（自拟）：“Gross, operating, and net margins are calculated separately as gross profit, operating income, and net income divided by revenue. Their three-year directions and percentage-point changes are [results], based on aligned fiscal-year statements.” 当前无数据。"
    },
    {
      "line": 715,
      "text": "中文：销售、一般及行政费用（selling, general, and administrative expenses，SG&A）包括销售推广和总部管理等运营开支，须按年报实际分类取数。同时算其同比、收入同比和 SG&A/收入比率；例如费用从 10 增到 11，收入从 100 增到 120，费用率反而从 10% 降至约 9.17%，不能只因金额上涨就称效率恶化。英文参考（自拟）：“I would compare SG&A growth with revenue growth and track SG&A as a percentage of revenue. This shows whether the expense grew faster or slower than sales, but does not alone establish efficiency.” 当前无数据。"
    },
    {
      "line": 733,
      "text": "中文：对齐经营活动现金流 CFO（卖货、提供服务及相关经营付款产生的净现金）三年期间，分开金额与同比。调查应收款、存货、应付等营运资本变动为何使它与净利润不同；§2.8.1 有交易和正负调节例。英文参考（自拟）：“Operating cash flow was [amount] in each fiscal year and changed by [percentage]. I would reconcile the trend with net income and working-capital movements.” 当前无数据。"
    },
    {
      "line": 937,
      "text": "中文：本题在源页的替代品组，但分类须先定边界：若分析整个智能手机行业，Android 手机通常是现有竞争者；若聚焦 iOS 生态，可作为替代方案（见 §2.5）。需按设备类别 / 地区 / 期间的份额序列，不把竞争技术出现直接当成 Apple 份额受损的证据。英文参考：“I would compare Apple's market share with a consistently defined Android or device-market series over time. The lecture slides contain no share data and cannot establish the impact.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 1021,
      "text": "中文：可选趋势、回归或情景，说明数据需求与模型限制。销售百分比法（percentage-of-sales method）是假定某项目随销售保持一定比例，例如应收款为收入的 10%，预测收入 1,050 时应收款为 105；这个比例本身不能凭空生成未来销售收入。若题目要求收入增长，先给历史趋势或销量、单价等驱动，再用比例法联动成本、资产与负债，不能把方法名当收入预测。英文参考：“Possible methods include trend extrapolation, regression with justified explanatory variables, percentage-of-sales assumptions, and scenarios. Method selection depends on data quality and structural stability.”"
    },
    {
      "line": 1075,
      "text": "| 这个比率是多少？ | 先区分报告日与期间：D/E 用同日期末值，ROE 例用平均权益；每股分母见 §2.1.1 |"
    },
    {
      "line": 1077,
      "text": "| 公司有什么优势 / 风险？ | SWOT 分内外部；五力先定市场边界，再追价格、成本或付款条件传导（§2.5） |"
    },
    {
      "line": 1102,
      "text": "| 市净率 | Price-to-book ratio (P/B) | Market price per share divided by book value per ordinary share at the stated date. | §2.1.1 |"
    },
    {
      "line": 1103,
      "text": "| 每股收益 | Earnings per share (EPS) | Earnings attributable to ordinary shareholders divided by the relevant weighted-average share count. | §2.1.1 |"
    },
    {
      "line": 1104,
      "text": "| 应收账款回收天数 | Days sales outstanding (DSO) | The stated days per year divided by receivables turnover, using consistent inputs. | §2.1.2 |"
    },
    {
      "line": 1105,
      "text": "| 留存收益 | Retained earnings | Accumulated earnings retained within equity after distributions and relevant adjustments; it is not a cash balance. | §2.6 |"
    },
    {
      "line": 1106,
      "text": "| 经营活动现金流 | Cash flow from operating activities (CFO) | Net cash from operating receipts and payments, distinct from accrual profit. | §2.7.1 |"
